================================================================================
SECTION 2: MAXPRI SOFTWARE ENGINEERING PRACTICES & CODING STANDARDS
================================================================================

This document details the core engineering standards, version control protocols, code review processes, and quality assurances expected from every Maxpri engineer.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.1 CODE QUALITY & ARCHITECTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Clean & Self-Documenting Code
   - Write clear variable, function, and file names that express intent.
   - Prefer self-explanatory code over excessive commenting; comment *why*, not *what*.
   - Keep functions focused on a single responsibility.

2. Minimal Dependency Overhead
   - Avoid introducing heavy npm packages for simple tasks that native Web APIs or lightweight utilities can achieve.
   - Leverage edge compute (Cloudflare Workers) and browser standards (HTML5, CSS custom properties, vanilla JS ES6+).

3. Security First
   - Never hardcode API keys, tokens, or credentials in client-side code or git repositories. Use Cloudflare Worker secret bindings and `.dev.vars` for local development.
   - Validate and sanitize all user input before processing or persisting.
   - Sanitize DOM manipulations to prevent XSS vulnerabilities.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.2 VERSION CONTROL & GIT WORKFLOW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Branch Naming Conventions
   - Feature branches: `feature/short-description` (e.g., `feature/voyager-auth`)
   - Bug fixes: `fix/short-description` (e.g., `fix/chat-widget-mobile`)
   - Documentation: `docs/short-description` (e.g., `docs/monodocs-update`)

2. Commit Messages
   - Format: `<type>: <short imperative summary>`
   - Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`
   - Subject lines should be under 50 characters and capitalized.
   - Example: `feat: add live status indicator to voyager agent`

3. Pull Requests & Code Reviews
   - All code pushed to production branches must pass review.
   - PRs must include a summary of changes, testing steps, and relevant screenshots if UI changes were made.
   - Verify local execution and edge worker compatibility before submitting PRs.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.3 PERFORMANCE & TESTING STANDARDS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Performance Budget
   - Maintain fast load times: page interactive time under 1.5 seconds.
   - Keep total initial asset size minimal. Use vector SVGs and optimized WebP/PNG assets.

2. Testing & Verification
   - Test UI responsiveness across mobile, tablet, and desktop viewports.
   - Test edge worker logic using `npx wrangler dev` or local mocks.
   - Verify all links, modals, and interactive widgets function error-free in modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.4 DEPLOYMENT & EDGE INFRASTRUCTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Maxpri applications utilize Cloudflare Workers for global routing and edge execution.
- Wrangler configurations (`wrangler.jsonc`) define worker routes, environment variables, and bindings.
- Always verify routing changes on staging worker preview deployments before promoting to production (`maxpritech.com`).
